course: dictionary
lesson: 15212
title: Doing things for no reason
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Senselessly tells you how something was done. Its clue is in the word inside it: sense means good reason or meaning. The ending -less means "without", so senselessly means without any good reason or purpose.
explain: Read this: «The boy senselessly kicked over the flower pots, even though they had done nothing to him.» Nobody gained anything, and no reason is given. Ask yourself: was there a good reason? If not, senselessly is the right word.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning: «The boy kicked over the pots for no good reason» still makes sense, so you have it right. Senselessly is often used for sad or serious acts, such as «senselessly wasted», where something valuable is thrown away for nothing.
fact: Senselessly is an adverb, a word that tells you how an action is done.
fact: «Senseless» is the adjective, as in «a senseless act». Senselessly is its adverb form.
fact: «Senselessly» means in a way that has no meaning, good reason or purpose.
fact: The ending -less means "without", so senseless means "without sense".
fact: «Senselessly wasted» means thrown away for no good purpose.
exercise: «The vandals senselessly smashed the bus shelter, although nobody had upset them.» What does senselessly mean here? | For a good reason, to keep people safe | *For no good reason | Happily, with a big smile | Very carefully and slowly
exercise: «She senselessly threw her new coat in the bin.» What does senselessly show about the action? | *That it had no good purpose | That she was going shopping | That the coat was too small for her | That she was very cold
exercise: Ella says senselessly means happily. What does senselessly actually mean? | *Without any good reason or purpose | Loudly, so everyone can hear | Happily and with a smile | Quickly, in a rush
test: «The workers senselessly cut down the old oak tree, when they could have walked around it.» Why is senselessly used in this sentence? | *Because there was no good reason to cut it down | Because it was the first day of spring | Because they were paid to do it | Because the oak tree was dying
test: «He senselessly wasted his birthday money on sweets he did not even like.» What does senselessly tell you about the spending? | It was a gift for a friend | It was wise and very careful | It was a planned surprise for his mum | *It was pointless, with no good purpose
exam: Which sentence shows an act done senselessly? | *He smashed the windows of the empty school for no reason at all. | They planted trees to shade the playground. | The firefighters carried the puppy out of the river. | We shared our lunch with a new friend.
